<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 144 0 R
/T (Whilst Support Coordinators \(SCs\) cannot prescribe or clinically assess what AT a participant needs, they play a major role in the process. The role of a Support Coordinator in AT prescription involves:)
/E (Whilst Support Coordinators \(SCs\) cannot prescribe or clinically assess what AT a participant needs, they play a major role in the process. The role of a Support Coordinator in AT prescription involves:)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
300 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Identifying AT needs within a plan: SCs work with the participant and family to clarify their goals and whether AT might benefit their goals. They can also help by checking if the AT is already funded in their NDIS plan or if an assessment is required.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Linking participants with the right professionals: SCs can connect participants to allied health providers who can assess, trial, and prescribe the AT.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
302 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Supporting evidence gathering: SCs coordinate reports, quotes, and documentation required for the AT application. They also ensure everything aligns with NDIS requirements.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
303 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Assisting with processes: SCs help submit requests for AT to the NDIS \(via myplace portal, email, or during plan reassessment\). They may also assist with explaining the difference between low-cost AT \(often bought directly with funding\) and complex AT \(which requires professional reports\).)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Implementation & follow-up: SCs support the participant to understand how to purchase approved AT. Alongside the Allied Health professional, they will also check in to ensure the equipment or technology is actually meeting their needs.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
